    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a1">

                <pb facs="0213" n="213" xml:id="pg213"/>

                <head>A.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 24, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that I am fully authorized by my government to enter into a convention with the
                    government of France in reference to the subject of privateering, the rights of
                    neutrals, and the matter of blockade.</p>
                <p>If, therefore, the government of his Imperial Majesty remains disposed to renew
                    negotiations upon these subjects, I shall be happy to have a conference with
                    your excellency at such time as your excellency may indicate.</p>
                <p>With great respect, I have the honor to be your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thouvenel</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
